WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:32.208
<b>The previous verse revealed</b>

2
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:39.250
<b>how surrendering our duties to Lord Krishna </b>
<b>offered with pure devotion bears blessed fruits.</b>

3
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:39.916
<b>Now,</b>

4
00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:43.375
<b>this verse presents us with the opposite scenario.</b>

5
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:46.500
<b>Here, when one neglects to</b>
<b>follow Krishna's divine teaching,</b>

6
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.250
<b>we examine the adverse consequences </b>
<b>that may unfold...</b>

7
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:57.708
<b>This verse speaks of those</b>

8
00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:03.500
<b>who ignore Krishna's teachings </b>
<b>and turn away from His wisdom.</b>

9
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.666
<b>Such people not only lose their knowledge,</b>

10
00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.500
<b>but</b>

11
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.791
<b>walk steadily towards their own destruction.</b>

12
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:13.833
<b>Now, it's vital to understand this point:</b>

13
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:19.416
<b>When people face destruction by </b>
<b>neglecting Krishna's teachings,</b>

14
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:25.166
<b>it's not because the Lord is punishing them.</b>

15
00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:28.666
<b>Krishna only wishes the best for all beings.</b>

16
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:31.208
<b>Think of it like this:</b>

17
00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:36.791
<b>Picture a plant that needs sunlight to grow.</b>

18
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:41.666
<b>If kept in darkness, it will slowly wither away.</b>

19
00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:44.208
<b>Is this the sun's punishment?</b>

20
00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:45.125
<b>No.</b>

21
00:01:45.125 --> 00:01:47.958
<b>The sun freely shares its rays with everyone,</b>

22
00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:50.291
<b>without any discrimination.</b>

23
00:01:50.291 --> 00:01:56.625
<b>If we bring that withering plant back into </b>
<b>sunlight before it's completely gone,</b>

24
00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>it will gradually restore itself to health.</b>

25
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.958
<b>Krishna's teachings are just </b>
<b>like these life-giving rays.</b>

26
00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:10.291
<b>If we fail to follow them, whether </b>
<b>knowingly or unknowingly,</b>

27
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:14.416
<b>the absence of this divine light will </b>
<b>naturally lead to our decline.</b>

28
00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:18.250
<b>Consider a student who becomes </b>
<b>frustrated with a difficult subject</b>

29
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.958
<b>and completely gives up on it.</b>

30
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:23.458
<b>Can they ever pass their exam?</b>

31
00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:24.625
<b>Clearly not.</b>

32
00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>While we easily grasp this principle </b>
<b>in matters of education,</b>

33
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:36.041
<b>we often become negligent and </b>
<b>arrogant when it comes to life itself.</b>

34
00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:41.958
<b>Some people, when struggling to </b>
<b>follow Vedic wisdom, grow frustrated</b>

35
00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:47.291
<b>and completely reject these </b>
<b>teachings, declaring them false.</b>

36
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:51.083
<b>This arrogance leads to their greatest mistake.</b>

37
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:54.875
<b>Isn't the purpose of life to achieve </b>
<b>eternal joy and liberation?</b>

38
00:02:54.875 --> 00:02:59.458
<b>This is exactly what Krishna's </b>
<b>teachings guide us toward -</b>

39
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.708
<b>the Bhagavad Gita –</b>

40
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:03.375
<b>By distancing ourselves from this wisdom,</b>

41
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:08.000
<b>we cut ourselves off from this life-giving light.</b>

42
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.958
<b>In such darkness, people make </b>
<b>countless mistakes,</b>

43
00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:13.333
<b>become trapped in karmic bonds,</b>

44
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.583
<b>and remain in suffering.</b>

45
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:17.916
<b>They might seem successful in worldly terms,</b>

46
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:21.791
<b>but their hearts remain empty and discontent.</b>

47
00:03:21.791 --> 00:03:25.125
<b>This divine knowledge is equally available to all.</b>

48
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:30.416
<b>The sun of wisdom continuously </b>
<b>shines for humanity's upliftment.</b>

49
00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:37.375
<b>All we need to do is step out of our </b>
<b>dark room into this radiant light.</b>

50
00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:39.250
<b>Life will flourish once again,</b>

51
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.375
<b>but remember -</b>

52
00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:43.791
<b>it takes faith and patience.</b>

53
00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:51.166
<b>Imagine</b>

54
00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:54.666
<b>having a map in life –</b>

55
00:03:54.666 --> 00:04:02.125
<b>a precious map leading to an invaluable treasure.</b>

56
00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:06.625
<b>Every path, every turn is clearly </b>
<b>marked on this divine guide.</b>

57
00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:08.375
<b>But what</b>

58
00:04:08.375 --> 00:04:14.250
<b>happens when you encounter </b>
<b>a mountain on your journey?</b>

59
00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.375
<b>Instead of persevering to cross it,</b>

60
00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:23.458
<b>you abandon the map, </b>
<b>searching for an easier route.</b>

61
00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:29.750
<b>You might stray from the path, </b>
<b>missing the treasure entirely.</b>

62
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.458
<b>and in the end,</b>

63
00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:33.625
<b>Some will turn back,</b>

64
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:36.625
<b>consoling themselves</b>

65
00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:42.000
<b>by claiming the treasure was merely a myth.</b>

66
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.250
<b>How clever we humans are –</b>

67
00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:54.458
<b>masters at concealing our failures by denying </b>
<b>truth or blaming others and circumstances.</b>

68
00:04:54.458 --> 00:04:56.541
<b>the Bhagavad Gita –</b>

69
00:04:56.541 --> 00:04:58.541
<b>all my teachings –</b>

70
00:04:58.541 --> 00:05:02.541
<b>consider them your map,</b>

71
00:05:02.541 --> 00:05:12.041
<b>guiding you step by step toward life's infinite </b>
<b>treasure of contentment and joy.</b>

72
00:05:12.041 --> 00:05:14.000
<b>Yes,</b>

73
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.583
<b>you will face mountains –</b>

74
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:22.625
<b>principles that seem complex,</b>

75
00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:28.083
<b>like performing duties without </b>
<b>attachment to results,</b>

76
00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:33.583
<b>treating your work as sacred offerings,</b>

77
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:39.125
<b>and surrendering all outcomes</b>
<b>to me with devotion.</b>

78
00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:51.208
<b>Don't let these challenges tempt you to seek </b>
<b>easier paths, for they may lead you astray.</b>

79
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:52.458
<b>Perhaps</b>

80
00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:54.875
<b>you're not among them,</b>

81
00:05:54.875 --> 00:06:04.333
<b>but if doubt ever clouds your mind </b>
<b>about the treasure's existence...</b>

82
00:06:04.333 --> 00:06:06.458
<b>remember this:</b>

83
00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:13.791
<b>Why would this map endure </b>
<b>thousands of years if it led nowhere?</b>

84
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:20.458
<b>Why would countless souls find </b>
<b>fulfillment following this very path?</b>

85
00:06:20.458 --> 00:06:29.208
<b>When progress seems slow, or you feel lost,</b>

86
00:06:29.208 --> 00:06:31.208
<b>remember -</b>

87
00:06:31.208 --> 00:06:34.000
<b>you hold the map.</b>

88
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.500
<b>Pick it up again, return to the true path.</b>

89
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:44.375
<b>I stand ready to help you always.</b>

90
00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:46.125
<b>But yes,</b>

91
00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:50.416
<b>walking this path - that you must do yourself.</b>

92
00:06:50.416 --> 00:06:54.625
<b>A teacher may offer endless guidance,</b>

93
00:06:54.625 --> 00:06:56.000
<b>but</b>

94
00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.541
<b>isn't it the student who must study and practice?</b>

95
00:07:01.541 --> 00:07:06.041
<b>After all, it is the student's life at stake.</b>

96
00:07:06.041 --> 00:07:12.250
<b>If you turn away from the sun of knowledge,</b>

97
00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:19.166
<b>won't you find yourself in the shadows </b>
<b>of ignorance, discontent, and sorrow?</b>

98
00:07:19.166 --> 00:07:20.791
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

99
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.666
<b>For any group to thrive,</b>

100
00:07:28.666 --> 00:07:30.375
<b>it is important</b>

101
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:38.250
<b>that each member's personal values </b>
<b>must align with the collective principles.</b>

102
00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:44.250
<b>If even one member begins to</b>
<b>think with opposing values,</b>

103
00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:51.375
<b>nothing can prevent discord and </b>
<b>division from taking root.</b>

104
00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:54.791
<b>Here's what becomes crucial –</b>

105
00:07:54.791 --> 00:08:02.250
<b>the leader must not only </b>
<b>establish the group's values</b>

106
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.041
<b>but</b>

107
00:08:03.041 --> 00:08:08.791
<b>also become an exemplary</b>
<b>model in following them.</b>

108
00:08:08.791 --> 00:08:13.291
<b>A family, too, is such a group.</b>

109
00:08:13.291 --> 00:08:21.541
<b>Can a family survive if selfishness </b>
<b>becomes its value?</b>

110
00:08:21.541 --> 00:08:23.166
<b>No.</b>

111
00:08:23.166 --> 00:08:29.500
<b>If people lose patience with each other,</b>

112
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:32.875
<b>can they live together in harmony?</b>

113
00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:34.666
<b>No.</b>

114
00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:35.875
<b>Patience,</b>

115
00:08:35.875 --> 00:08:37.375
<b>selflessness,</b>

116
00:08:37.375 --> 00:08:39.125
<b>mutual support –</b>

117
00:08:39.125 --> 00:08:45.583
<b>these values are essential for a family's success.</b>

118
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:52.250
<b>If family members turn </b>
<b>away from these values' light,</b>

119
00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:57.000
<b>it's like turning away from the sun itself.</b>

120
00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:04.541
<b>And in doing so, only shadows of </b>
<b>discord and conflict will appear.</b>

121
00:09:04.541 --> 00:09:06.708
<b>For instance,</b>

122
00:09:06.708 --> 00:09:16.125
<b>what happens when family members </b>
<b>focus solely on personal desires?</b>

123
00:09:16.125 --> 00:09:22.666
<b>If children begin this pattern, </b>
<b>they'll forget family values entirely.</b>

124
00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:25.333
<b>If parents become selfish,</b>

125
00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:32.041
<b>they'll neglect their children. </b>
<b>The bonds of love will fade.</b>

126
00:09:32.041 --> 00:09:39.916
<b>And it's this mutual love that holds </b>
<b>a family together, like an unbreakable bond.</b>

127
00:09:39.916 --> 00:09:43.250
<b>But as I said,</b>

128
00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:49.208
<b>establishing and personally </b>
<b>following family values</b>

129
00:09:49.208 --> 00:09:53.166
<b>is crucial for the family elders.</b>

130
00:09:53.166 --> 00:09:55.666
<b>For example,</b>

131
00:09:55.666 --> 00:10:02.458
<b>if you tell your children to have patience and faith,</b>

132
00:10:02.458 --> 00:10:07.333
<b>but lose your composure over small mistakes</b>

133
00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:10.208
<b>and scold them,</b>

134
00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:17.833
<b>then this gap between your words </b>
<b>and actions will become glaringly apparent.</b>

135
00:10:17.833 --> 00:10:22.916
<b>Your words will ring hollow.</b>

136
00:10:22.916 --> 00:10:26.750
<b>If you seek a treasure,</b>

137
00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.958
<b>having a written map isn't enough –</b>

138
00:10:30.958 --> 00:10:37.166
<b>you must actually walk </b>
<b>the path it shows in real life.</b>

139
00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:38.791
<b>Remember,</b>

140
00:10:38.791 --> 00:10:40.166
<b>this Gita</b>

141
00:10:40.166 --> 00:10:47.375
<b>is a map to infinite love and </b>
<b>contentment in family life,</b>

142
00:10:47.375 --> 00:10:55.458
<b>suggesting paths of patience, </b>
<b>selflessness, and devotion.</b>

143
00:10:55.458 --> 00:11:03.500
<b>But if you, as a family elder, stray from this path,</b>

144
00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:08.791
<b>your family following behind </b>
<b>will lose their way too.</b>

145
00:11:08.791 --> 00:11:10.083
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

146
00:11:10.083 --> 00:11:12.166
<b>Understand this path,</b>

147
00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:15.166
<b>and keep walking.</b>

148
00:11:15.166 --> 00:11:16.916
<b>Don't lose your way.</b>

149
00:11:21.666 --> 00:11:27.791
<b>View your workplace as a small universe,</b>

150
00:11:27.791 --> 00:11:36.958
<b>where each person carries their </b>
<b>own roles, desires, and perspectives.</b>

151
00:11:36.958 --> 00:11:39.458
<b>In such a diverse environment,</b>

152
00:11:39.458 --> 00:11:49.416
<b>if we overlook the spiritual principles </b>
<b>of cooperation, empathy, and selflessness,</b>

153
00:11:49.416 --> 00:11:54.666
<b>negativity and stagnation will spread.</b>

154
00:11:54.666 --> 00:12:00.875
<b>When self-interest and </b>
<b>rivalry overshadow cooperation,</b>

155
00:12:00.875 --> 00:12:06.333
<b>all trust will crumble,</b>

156
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:13.833
<b>and trust is absolutely essential </b>
<b>for a team to function smoothly.</b>

157
00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:18.291
<b>Each person will fulfill their role effectively</b>

158
00:12:18.291 --> 00:12:25.541
<b>only when they believe that everyone </b>
<b>else is doing the same.</b>

159
00:12:25.541 --> 00:12:31.041
<b>The responsibility to create such a positive </b>
<b>atmosphere rests on everyone's shoulders –</b>

160
00:12:31.041 --> 00:12:40.333
<b>both those in leadership positions </b>
<b>and their fellow team members.</b>

161
00:12:40.333 --> 00:12:47.041
<b>While leaders must let </b>
<b>go of control and ownership</b>

162
00:12:47.041 --> 00:12:50.541
<b>to understand their people with an open mind,</b>

163
00:12:50.541 --> 00:12:57.833
<b>every colleague must also </b>
<b>abandon personal self-interest.</b>

164
00:12:57.833 --> 00:13:02.875
<b>And if some colleagues struggle with this,</b>

165
00:13:02.875 --> 00:13:09.458
<b>it falls upon senior leaders to practice patience,</b>

166
00:13:09.458 --> 00:13:15.041
<b>help them understand and guide them.</b>

167
00:13:15.041 --> 00:13:16.916
<b>Selflessness,</b>

168
00:13:16.916 --> 00:13:20.500
<b>mutual cooperation, and patience –</b>

169
00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:28.791
<b>these are the three torches that illuminate the </b>
<b>path to success in a professional environment.</b>

170
00:13:28.791 --> 00:13:36.291
<b>If these lights dim, the </b>
<b>organization will lose its way.</b>

171
00:13:36.291 --> 00:13:40.833
<b>Keep these values burning bright within you,</b>

172
00:13:40.833 --> 00:13:44.291
<b>and if you see someone else's light flickering,</b>

173
00:13:44.291 --> 00:13:48.375
<b>use your flame to reignite theirs.</b>

174
00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:53.000
<b>This, after all, is what true cooperation means.</b>

175
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.041
<b>Reflect on this wisdom.</b>

